extends layout.pug

block meta
    meta(name="description" content="Support groups and resources for parents with children dealing with addiction in Spokane, WA. Find hope and education through PAL, Awaken Spokane, Gabriel’s Challenge, and more.")
    
    script(type="application/ld+json").
      {
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "CollectionPage",
        "name": "Support for Parents of Addicted Children in Spokane, WA",
        "description": "Comprehensive resources for parents, grandparents, and families dealing with a loved one's addiction or loss due to addiction in the Spokane area.",
        "url": "https://www.getsoberspokane.com/parents-addiction-support.html",
        "about": {
          "@type": "Thing",
          "name": "Family Addiction Support and Recovery Resources"
        }
      }

block content
    //- Hero Section
    header.page-hero
      .container.px-4.px-lg-5
        h1 Support for Parents of Addicted Children in Spokane
        p.lead Resources, support groups, and hope for families navigating the journey of a loved one's addiction.
        .hero-badges
          .hero-badge
            i.bi.bi-people-fill
            span Local Support Groups
          .hero-badge
            i.bi.bi-heart-fill
            span Hope & Healing
          .hero-badge
            i.bi.bi-book-fill
            span Education & Tools

    //- Main Content
    section.page-section
      .container.px-4.px-lg-5
        .row.justify-content-center
          .col-lg-10
            h2.text-primary.mt-0 A Message of Support for Parents
            p.mb-4 Dealing with a child's addiction is a journey no parent ever hopes to take. It can be a road filled with grief, even while your child is still living. Whether you are raising grandchildren, navigating the complex systems of care, or simply trying to love your child while protecting your own sanity, you are not alone. 
            
            p.mb-5 Spokane has a community of parents and organizations dedicated to walking alongside you. Below are resources specifically for parents, grandparents, and family members affected by substance use disorder.

            //- Local Spokane Resources
            h2.text-primary.mt-5 Local Spokane Support & Resources
            p.mb-4 These organizations offer direct support, education, and community for families in the Spokane area.

            .table-responsive
              table.table.table-bordered.table-striped.mt-3
                thead.table-dark
                  tr
                    th Organization
                    th Focus
                    th Details & Contact
                tbody
                  tr
                    td Parents of Addicted Loved Ones (PAL)
                    td Education & Peer Support
                    td 
                      strong Free weekly groups 
                      | led by trained facilitators who have walked the same path. PAL provides evidence-based practices for dealing with issues from setting boundaries to delayed emotional growth. Open to parents, spouses, and family members (18+).
                      br
                      a(href='https://palgroup.org', target='_blank', rel='noopener') palgroup.org
                  tr
                    td Awaken Spokane
                    td Faith, Community & Podcast
                    td 
                      | A Christ-centered community helping people encounter God, experience freedom, and embrace community in real, everyday life. Awaken Spokane offers practical teaching, worship, prayer, and connection for individuals and families seeking hope, healing, and purpose. Meets Sundays at 10 AM at Shaw Middle School.
                      br
                      strong Podcast: 
                      | Available on Spotify for encouraging messages rooted in faith and real-life application.
                  tr
                    td Gabriel’s Challenge
                    td Community Connection & Resource Access
                    td 
                      | A community-driven effort focused on prevention, connection, and closing system gaps. Their Community Education and Empowerment Center at Northtown Mall is not a service clinic, but a space for connection, conversation, coordination, resource information, partner engagement, and youth and family voice.
                  tr
                    td Community-Minded Enterprises
                    td Recovery Support & Community Resources
                    td 
                      | A nonprofit committed to building healthier, stronger communities by helping individuals and families access support, stability, and opportunity. Through resources like Recovery Café and grant-funded programs, Community-Minded Enterprises helps people in recovery overcome barriers to education, employment, and long-term wellness.
                  tr
                    td Partners with Families and Children
                    td Family-Centered Treatment
                    td 
                      | Offers outpatient treatment services and family counseling aimed at restoring balance and healing the family unit.
                      br
                      a(href='tel:+15094734351') (509) 473-4351
                  tr
                    td Spokane Falls Recovery Center
                    td Family Therapy Programs
                    td 
                      | Provides specialized family therapy designed to foster communication and support family members during a loved one's recovery process.
                      br
                      a(href='tel:+18449622775') (844) 962-2775
                  tr
                    td Maddie's Place
                    td Support for New Families
                    td 
                      | A recovery nursery for families and substance-exposed newborns, providing a holistic approach to healing and stability.
                      br
                      a(href='https://maddiesplace.org', target='_blank', rel='noopener') maddiesplace.org

            //- Support for Loss
            h2.text-primary.mt-5 Support for Loss and Grief
            p.mb-4 For parents who have lost a child to addiction, the pain is unimaginable. Finding a community of others who understand this specific type of loss can be a vital part of healing.
            ul.mb-5
              li 
                strong Gabriel’s Challenge: 
                | Founded on the experience of loss, Kitara Johnson-Jones provides a space for community conversation and support.
              li 
                strong GRASP (Grief Recovery After a Substance Passing): 
                | A national organization with local chapters providing help, compassion, and understanding for those who have lost a loved one to substance use. 
                a(href='http://grasphelp.org', target='_blank', rel='noopener') grasphelp.org
              li 
                strong The Compassionate Friends: 
                | While not addiction-specific, they offer extensive support for parents who have experienced the death of a child.

            //- National Resources
            h2.text-primary.mt-5 National Resources & Education
            .row.gx-4.gy-4.mb-5
                .col-md-6
                    .card.h-100.border-0.shadow-sm
                        .card-body
                            h5 Partnership to End Addiction
                            p Provides personalized support, a helpline for parents, and evidence-based resources to navigate your child's recovery journey.
                            a(href='https://drugfree.org', target='_blank', rel='noopener') drugfree.org
                .col-md-6
                    .card.h-100.border-0.shadow-sm
                        .card-body
                            h5 SAMHSA’s National Helpline
                            p Confidential, 24/7, 365-day-a-year treatment referral and information service for families.
                            a(href='tel:18006624357') 1-800-662-HELP (4357)
                .col-md-6
                    .card.h-100.border-0.shadow-sm
                        .card-body
                            h5 Al-Anon / Alateen
                            p Support groups for friends and families of individuals struggling with alcoholism.
                            a(href='https://al-anon.org', target='_blank', rel='noopener') al-anon.org
                .col-md-6
                    .card.h-100.border-0.shadow-sm
                        .card-body
                            h5 Nar-Anon
                            p A 12-step program for those affected by someone else’s drug addiction.
                            a(href='https://nar-anon.org', target='_blank', rel='noopener') nar-anon.org

            //- FAQ Section
            h2.text-primary.mt-5 Frequently Asked Questions for Parents
            .accordion#parentFaqAccordion.mb-5
                .accordion-item.border-0.mb-3.shadow-sm(style="border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden;")
                    h3.accordion-header#pf1heading
                        button.accordion-button.fw-semibold(type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#pf1" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="pf1") How do I set boundaries with my addicted adult child?
                    #pf1.accordion-collapse.collapse.show(aria-labelledby="pf1heading" data-bs-parent="#parentFaqAccordion")
                        .accordion-body.text-muted Setting boundaries is about protecting your own well-being and not enabling the addiction. Resources like PAL (Parents of Addicted Loved Ones) offer specific tools and evidence-based practices to help you establish and maintain healthy boundaries.
                .accordion-item.border-0.mb-3.shadow-sm(style="border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden;")
                    h3.accordion-header#pf2heading
                        button.accordion-button.collapsed.fw-semibold(type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#pf2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pf2") Where can grandparents raising grandchildren find support in Spokane?
                    #pf2.accordion-collapse.collapse(aria-labelledby="pf2heading" data-bs-parent="#parentFaqAccordion")
                        .accordion-body.text-muted Many local support groups, including PAL and faith-based groups like Awaken Spokane, are open to grandparents and offer a space for shared experience and practical advice for navigating the family dynamics of addiction.
                .accordion-item.border-0.mb-3.shadow-sm(style="border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden;")
                    h3.accordion-header#pf3heading
                        button.accordion-button.collapsed.fw-semibold(type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#pf3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pf3") Is there any financial help for my child's recovery-related barriers?
                    #pf3.accordion-collapse.collapse(aria-labelledby="pf3heading" data-bs-parent="#parentFaqAccordion")
                        .accordion-body.text-muted Organizations like Community-Minded Enterprises in Spokane lead grant programs that can help reduce barriers for education or employment opportunities for people in recovery, assisting with the long-term stability of your child.

    //- Call to Action
    section.page-section.bg-primary.text-white.text-center
      .container.px-4.px-lg-5
        h2.mb-4 You Don't Have to Walk This Road Alone
        p.mb-4 Reach out to a local support group or contact us for more information on finding the right resources for your family.
        a.btn.btn-light.btn-xl(href='index.html#contact') Contact Us
